# Export rules for the public snapshot sync.
#
# The public GitHub repo receives a *curated snapshot* built with `git archive`,
# which honours these rules. `.gitignore` does NOT help here: it has no effect on
# files that are already tracked.
#
# Why `.gitea/` is excluded: it holds this instance's CI configuration, which is
# useless off this instance and carries the internal clone URL and org path. The
# automated public-tree check in ci.yml would otherwise fail on it.
#
# `.github/` is deliberately NOT excluded. This repository ships no GitHub CI
# (deployment is Gitea-only by decision), so there is nothing to keep -- but the
# rule is stated so nobody adds an exclusion that silently strips a future
# .github/ directory.
.gitea/          export-ignore
